{"id":"mahabharata-2-065","work":"mahabharata","part":2,"partName":"सभापर्व","partNameEn":"Sabha Parva","unit":65,"title":"पञ्चषष्टितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 65 · Dhritarashtra restores the kingdom","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks Dhritarashtra's command. The old king begs him to forget the wrongs of the game, restores to him all he lost, and sends him back to Indraprastha, and the Pandavas depart with Draupadi.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನ ಆಜ್ಞೆ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಜೂಜಿನ ಅನ್ಯಾಯಗಳನ್ನು ಮರೆತುಬಿಡೆಂದು ವೃದ್ಧರಾಜನು ಬೇಡಿ ಸೋತದ್ದೆಲ್ಲವನ್ನೂ ಮರಳಿಸಿ ಇಂದ್ರಪ್ರಸ್ಥಕ್ಕೆ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವರು ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹೊರಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर धृतराष्ट्र की आज्ञा पूछते हैं। वृद्ध राजा उनसे द्यूत के अन्याय भूल जाने की विनती करते हैं, हारा हुआ सब लौटाकर उन्हें इन्द्रप्रस्थ भेज देते हैं, और पाण्डव द्रौपदी के साथ विदा होते हैं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ధృతరాష్ట్రుని ఆజ్ఞ అడుగుతాడు. జూదంలోని అన్యాయాలను మరచిపొమ్మని వృద్ధరాజు వేడుకొని ఓడినదంతా తిరిగి ఇచ్చి ఇంద్రప్రస్థానికి పంపుతాడు; పాండవులు ద్రౌపదితో బయలుదేరుతారు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரர் திருதராஷ்டிரனின் ஆணையைக் கேட்கிறார். சூதின் அநீதிகளை மறந்துவிடுமாறு முதிய மன்னன் வேண்டி, இழந்தவை அனைத்தையும் திருப்பித் தந்து இந்திரப்ரஸ்தத்துக்கு அனுப்புகிறான்; பாண்டவர்கள் திரௌபதியுடன் புறப்படுகிறார்கள்.","ml":"ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരുടെ കല്പന എന്തെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ചൂതുകളിയിലെ അന്യായങ്ങൾ മറക്കണമെന്ന് വൃദ്ധരാജാവ് അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; നഷ്ടപ്പെട്ടതെല്ലാം തിരികെ നൽകി ഇന്ദ്രപ്രസ്ഥത്തിലേക്ക് അയയ്ക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവർ ദ്രൗപദിയോടൊപ്പം പുറപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 2.65; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Apr 19 2006","sections":[{"title":"द्यूतपर्व","titleEn":"Dyuta Parva (The dice game)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"राजन्किं करवामस्ते प्रशाध्यस्मांस्त्वमीश्वरः ।\nनित्यं हि स्थातुमिच्छामस्तव भारत शासने ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, what shall we do for you? Command us, you are our lord. We always wish to remain under your rule, Bharata."}},{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"अजातशत्रो भद्रं ते अरिष्टं स्वस्ति गच्छत ।\nअनुज्ञाताः सहधनाः स्वराज्यमनुशासत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born without an enemy, may you be well. Go safely with my blessing, and rule your own kingdom together with your wealth."}},{"n":3,"text":"इदं त्वेवावबोद्धव्यं वृद्धस्य मम शासनम् ।\nधिया निगदितं कृत्स्नं पथ्यं निःश्रेयसं परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But understand this command of mine, an old man's, spoken with thought, all of it wholesome and supremely good."}},{"n":4,"text":"वेत्थ त्वं तात धर्माणां गतिं सूक्ष्मां युधिष्ठिर ।\nविनीतोऽसि महाप्राज्ञ वृद्धानां पर्युपासिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, my son, you know the subtle course of dharmas. You are well disciplined, greatly wise, and you have served your elders."}},{"n":5,"text":"यतो बुद्धिस्ततः शान्तिः प्रशमं गच्छ भारत ।\nनादारौ क्रमते शस्त्रं दारौ शस्त्रं निपात्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where there is understanding there is peace; be calm, Bharata. A weapon does not strike one who has no foe; it is used where there is one."}},{"n":6,"text":"न वैराण्यभिजानन्ति गुणान्पश्यन्ति नागुणान् ।\nविरोधं नाधिगच्छन्ति ये त उत्तमपूरुषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best men do not take note of enmities; they see virtues, not faults, and they do not enter conflict."}},{"n":7,"text":"संवादे परुषाण्याहुर्युधिष्ठिर नराधमाः ।\nप्रत्याहुर्मध्यमास्त्वेतानुक्ताः परुषमुत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, the lowest men speak harshly in conversation; the middling answer harsh words with a harsh reply."}},{"n":8,"text":"नैवोक्ता नैव चानुक्ता अहिताः परुषा गिरः ।\nप्रतिजल्पन्ति वै धीराः सदा उत्तमपूरुषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the steadfast, the best of men, never answer unfriendly harsh words, whether spoken or not."}},{"n":9,"text":"स्मरन्ति सुकृतान्येव न वैराणि कृतान्यपि ।\nसन्तः प्रतिविजानन्तो लब्ध्वा प्रत्ययमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Good men remember only the good done to them, not the enmities done, and they act when they have gained self-confidence."}},{"n":10,"text":"तथाचरितमार्येण त्वयास्मिन्सत्समागमे ।\nदुर्योधनस्य पारुष्यं तत्तात हृदि मा कृथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You acted like a noble man in this meeting of the good; do not keep Duryodhana's harshness in your heart, son."}},{"n":11,"text":"मातरं चैव गान्धारीं मां च त्वद्गुणकाङ्क्षिणम् ।\nउपस्थितं वृद्धमन्धं पितरं पश्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look on your mother Gandhari and on me, your old blind father, who long for your good qualities and stand before you."}},{"n":12,"text":"प्रेक्षापूर्वं मया द्यूतमिदमासीदुपेक्षितम् ।\nमित्राणि द्रष्टुकामेन पुत्राणां च बलाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I let this gambling go on, having foreseen it, wishing to see my friends and to measure my sons' strength and weakness."}},{"n":13,"text":"अशोच्याः कुरवो राजन्येषां त्वमनुशासिता ।\nमन्त्री च विदुरो धीमान्सर्वशास्त्रविशारदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kurus need not be mourned, king, since you rule them, and the wise Vidura is their minister, skilled in all scriptures."}},{"n":14,"text":"त्वयि धर्मोऽर्जुने वीर्यं भीमसेने पराक्रमः ।\nश्रद्धा च गुरुशुश्रूषा यमयोः पुरुषाग्र्ययोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In you is dharma, in Arjuna valor, in Bhimasena might, and in the twins, best of men, devotion and service of elders."}},{"n":15,"text":"अजातशत्रो भद्रं ते खाण्डवप्रस्थमाविश ।\nभ्रातृभिस्तेऽस्तु सौभ्रात्रं धर्मे ते धीयतां मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born without an enemy, may you fare well. Go to Khandavaprastha. Let brotherliness be with your brothers and let your mind be set on dharma."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"इत्युक्तो भरतश्रेष्ठो धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nकृत्वार्यसमयं सर्वं प्रतस्थे भ्रातृभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, Yudhishthira, best of the Bharatas and king of dharma, made all the noble agreements and set out with his brothers."}},{"n":17,"text":"ते रथान्मेघसंकाशानास्थाय सह कृष्णया ।\nप्रययुर्हृष्टमनस इन्द्रप्रस्थं पुरोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mounting chariots like clouds, with Krishna, they went gladly to Indraprastha, the best of cities."}}]}]}